### Ziptrrip Todo API — REST Client requests
### Open this file in VS Code with the "REST Client" extension installed,
### run `npm run dev` first, then click "Send Request" above each block.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:3000/api

### 1. List all todos
GET {{baseUrl}}/todos

### 2. List only active (incomplete) todos
GET {{baseUrl}}/todos?filter=active

### 3. List only completed todos
GET {{baseUrl}}/todos?filter=completed

### 4. Create a todo
# @name createTodo
POST {{baseUrl}}/todos
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Prepare demo for Ziptrrip interview",
  "description": "Walk through CRUD APIs and both pages",
  "priority": "high",
  "dueDate": "2026-09-10"
}

### 5. Get a single todo by id (replace 1 with a real id from step 4's response)
GET {{baseUrl}}/todos/1

### 6. Update a todo (partial update — only send fields you want to change)
PUT {{baseUrl}}/todos/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "completed": true
}

### 7. Rename + reprioritize a todo
PUT {{baseUrl}}/todos/1
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": "Prepare demo for Ziptrrip interview (updated)",
  "priority": "medium"
}

### 8. Delete a todo
DELETE {{baseUrl}}/todos/1

### 9. Error case: creating a todo with an empty title (expect 400)
POST {{baseUrl}}/todos
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "title": ""
}

### 10. Error case: fetching a non-existent todo (expect 404)
GET {{baseUrl}}/todos/999999
